id: low-sky
name: Low Sky
kind: high
highRank: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Open air. Nothing up here does anything to you - it is the Battle Environment below
  that stops reaching you, which is the whole of what being airborne is worth.
text: >
  Low Sky Environment: High above the landscape, where nothing interferes with the
  battle.

  Hardness Rank: N/A

  Effects: N/A

---

# "Where nothing interferes with the battle", and the entry means it: no Hardness Rank, no
# effects. The Normal Light Level and the Standard Environment have the same shape and
# exist for the same reason - "N/A" is a rule with a name.
#
# What it is worth is what it takes away rather than what it adds. A character in the Low
# Sky is out of the Lava, out of the Bog and out of the water, because a High Environment
# is layered above the Battle Environment and the Environment below stops reaching them.
#
# Battle Weather still does. It is the only one of the four that does not say otherwise,
# which is the difference between the sky and everything above it.
#
# No statements, so the registry drops the program.
